# Stitch screens are the layout source

Before building or restyling any Attend Pal screen:

1. Call Stitch `list_screens` for project `16824782504686943603`.
2. Download that step’s screenshot and HTML with `download_file`. View them before writing code.
3. Match the Stitch layout, visible copy, spacing, and controls. Do not invent a simpler screen or paraphrase the labels.
4. Result states are their own screens. Download each one before building that state: Session Link Inactive, Already Checked In, Check-in Isn't Open, Outside Class Area, and Identity Check Failed.
5. Drop the Tailwind CDN, Google font links, and external image URLs. Use this repo’s design tokens and `lucide-react` (`Copy`, not `ContentCopy`).
6. Keep sample data only on Pass 1. Remove names like “Dr. Mensah” when wiring Pass 2. Keep the Stitch layout and static sentences.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — a short heading in place of the Stitch inactive screen
<h1>Link no longer active</h1>
<p>Ask your lecturer for a new link or code.</p>

// ✅ GOOD — Stitch “Result: Session Link Inactive”: kiosk header, Session Closed,
// “This link is no longer active”, verification tip, course rows, Scan new QR code
```
